    "created_at": "2023-02-22T18:59:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-22T18:59:14Z",
    "body": "I had the same issue, but found switching the Encoding value to \"oem\" solved my issue.\r\n\r\nFirst, I validated the font was rendering properly by running `starship preset nerd-font-symbols`, then I copy and pasted the terminal output directly into the starship.toml configuration, typed a command `ls` for example and it printed out the characters properly.\r\n\r\nTo fix, when setting a preset, use something similar to this:\r\n`starship preset nerd-font-symbols | Out-File -Encoding oem ~/.config/starship.toml`\r\n\r\nThis should work if the symbols are already rendering properly.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
